<h3>Repackaging A Linux Install Iso</h3>
<pre><code># Mount ISO
mkdir -p /mnt/linux
mount -o loop /tmp/linux-install.iso /mnt/linux</code></pre>
<pre><code># Copy contents to a working directory
cd /mnt/
tar -cvf =E2=80=94 Linux | (cd /var/tmp &amp;&amp; tar -xf =E2=80=94 )</cod=
e></pre>
<pre><code># Make your changes and repackage (on Debian use genisoimage). -=
c passes the name of the file that will be created
cd /var/tmp/linux
mkisofs -o ../your-new.iso -b isolinux/isolinux.bin -c isolinux/boot.cat -n=
o-emul-boot -boot-load-size 4 -boot-info-table -J -R -V Your Disk Name Here=
 .</code></pre>
